Now that 3.0 has been posted, there is a need for your help
in digging up bugs.  There are bugs in it.  We already discovered
over a dozen, and some good people have discovered more and alerted us
to them.  These are being fixed (by us, or by people who mail a fix 
to a bug they uncover), and soon we will post the first official 
bug-fix patch.

But we need your help in this bug-chase.  Please send your bug-alerts 
and fixes to the address provided in the README file.  Let's get as
many of these bugs fixed as soon as possible, before we turn to the
fun of adding new features.

For the development team,

-Izchak


